# Vercel Speed Insights Configuration - Report

## Summary
After reviewing the codebase and fetching the latest Vercel Speed Insights documentation, I found that **Vercel Speed Insights is already properly installed and configured** in this project.

## Project Type
This is a **static HTML website** (not a Next.js, React, or other framework-based project).

## Current Implementation Status ✓

### Files Verified
All HTML pages in the project have Speed Insights correctly implemented:
- `index.html`
- `nosotros.html`
- `contacto.html`

### Implementation Details
Each HTML file contains the correct Speed Insights initialization code in the `<head>` section:

```html
<!-- Vercel Web Analytics & Speed Insights -->
<script>
  window.si = window.si || function () { (window.siq = window.siq || []).push(arguments); };
</script>
<script defer src="/_vercel/speed-insights/script.js"></script>
```

This matches the **official Vercel documentation** for static HTML/vanilla JavaScript projects (as fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart on September 11, 2026).

## Documentation Verification
✓ Fetched latest documentation from: https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart
✓ Confirmed implementation matches official guidelines for static HTML sites
✓ Verified all pages include the tracking scripts

## Key Implementation Points

1. **No package installation required**: Static HTML sites don't need the `@vercel/speed-insights` npm package. The tracking is handled via script tags.

2. **Script initialization**: The first script (`window.si = window.si || function()...`) initializes the Speed Insights queue.

3. **Deferred loading**: The second script loads the tracking code from `/_vercel/speed-insights/script.js` with the `defer` attribute for optimal performance.

4. **Automatic route collection**: When deployed to Vercel, the platform automatically includes routes at `/_vercel/speed-insights/*` to collect performance metrics.

5. **Web Analytics included**: The site also has Vercel Web Analytics properly configured alongside Speed Insights.

## No Changes Required
Since the implementation is already complete and correct, no code changes were necessary. The Speed Insights functionality will work automatically once the site is deployed to Vercel, and performance data will begin collecting when users visit the site.

## Additional Notes
- The site is configured with proper CSP headers in `vercel.json`
- All three pages (home, about, contact) have identical Speed Insights implementation
- The implementation follows best practices with deferred script loading for performance
